tle":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no."}],"title":"MXLPedal","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPedal"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/id":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"title":"id","url":"\/docume